WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.193 --> 00:00:14.143
For a minute we all stared at Tufty.

2
00:00:15.344 --> 00:00:16.946
Then we burst out laughing.

3
00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:23.551
can't believe Tufty made that subway sound!"

4
00:00:23.891 --> 00:00:24.652
said Josh.

5
00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:28.195
"It sounded like a real subway train!"

6
00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:29.276
said Molly.

7
00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:35.327
"But Aunt Lydia said that Tufty has never said a word," said Jenny.

8
00:00:35.347 --> 00:00:40.209
"He didn't say a word," I pointed out.

9
00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:42.090
"He made a sound.

10
00:00:43.171 --> 00:00:45.672
He roared like a subway train!"

11
00:00:45.692 --> 00:00:50.014
"Aunt Lydia lived near the subway," said Josh.

12
00:00:51.255 --> 00:00:54.117
"Maybe Tufty learned to imitate the sound of the trains."

13
00:00:55.557 --> 00:00:57.518
Mrs. O'Donnell looked worried.

14
00:00:57.538 --> 00:01:01.461
"I hope he never does that again," she said.

15
00:01:01.481 --> 00:01:04.923
"We can't keep a noisy parrot in our apartment.

16
00:01:05.443 --> 00:01:07.265
Our neighbors will get very annoyed."

17
00:01:07.285 --> 00:01:13.048
"We have to keep Tufty, Mom," said Molly.

18
00:01:13.068 --> 00:01:16.010
"He's so cute and friendly!

19
00:01:16.131 --> 00:01:18.132
And he's going to help me get better!"

20
00:01:19.473 --> 00:01:21.414
Tufty began cleaning his feathers.

21
00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.736
"He's quiet now," said Jenny.

22
00:01:24.756 --> 00:01:29.720
"It's hard to believe he made such a loud noise," said Josh.

23
00:01:31.228 --> 00:01:32.910
Molly's mom shook her head.

24
00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.733
"I just hope it doesn't happen again," she said.

25
00:01:39.315 --> 00:01:42.658
We watched as she began to take food out of a big cooler.

26
00:01:42.678 --> 00:01:46.321
"We use this cooler for camping," she said.

27
00:01:46.341 --> 00:01:50.444
"But during a blackout, it really comes in handy too."

28
00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:55.728
Molly's mom had filled the cooler with ice from the market.

29
00:01:57.109 --> 00:02:00.012
She took out fruit, juice, and some eggs.

30
00:02:01.836 --> 00:02:04.257
"These eggs are still cold," she said.

31
00:02:04.277 --> 00:02:08.500
"I'll have to throw them out if the refrigerator doesn't come back on soon."

32
00:02:10.061 --> 00:02:13.623
Molly's mom made us a snack of peanut butter, crackers, and fruit.

33
00:02:14.783 --> 00:02:15.884
We all drank some juice.

34
00:02:16.945 --> 00:02:19.206
Tufty sat on top of his cage and watched us.

35
00:02:21.087 --> 00:02:25.169
Then he flew down and pecked at cracker crumbs that fell on the floor.

36
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.252
Luckily, he didn't make any more subway sounds.

37
00:02:30.308 --> 00:02:35.613
Suddenly Caswell called from the living room, "Guess what I'm doing!"

38
00:02:35.633 --> 00:02:38.996
"Uh-oh," said Molly's mother.

39
00:02:40.297 --> 00:02:42.819
Josh, Jenny, and I hurried into the living room.

40
00:02:45.982 --> 00:02:47.863
Caswell was peering out of the window.

41
00:02:49.004 --> 00:02:51.166
Beside him was the carton of eggs that Mrs.

42
00:02:51.266 --> 00:02:53.568
O'Donnell had been storing in the cooler.

43
00:02:55.029 --> 00:02:57.772
Several of the eggs were missing.

44
00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.541
"Hey!" yelled a man from the street below.

45
00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:09.023
"Who's dropping raw eggs on the sidewalk?"

46
00:03:10.284 --> 00:03:12.205
Mrs. O'Donnell ran into the room.

47
00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.346
"Caswell, what are you doing?"

48
00:03:14.747 --> 00:03:15.327
she cried.

49
00:03:15.347 --> 00:03:19.869
"I'm making fried eggs," said Caswell.

50
00:03:19.889 --> 00:03:26.693
"Iggy's mom said it was hot enough to fry eggs on the sidewalk."

51
00:03:27.013 --> 00:03:28.094
I started laughing.

52
00:03:28.114 --> 00:03:30.435
"That's one way to cook them!"

53
00:03:30.896 --> 00:03:31.296
I said.

54
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.724
"Caswell, she didn't mean you could really fry eggs on the sidewalk," said Josh.

55
00:03:37.744 --> 00:03:41.766
"That's just an expression," I explained.

56
00:03:41.786 --> 00:03:45.829
"It means that it's very, very hot outside."

57
00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.911
Caswell looked disappointed.

58
00:03:48.931 --> 00:03:52.854
"So the eggs won't really cook?"

59
00:03:54.475 --> 00:03:57.657
"No, and you had better clean up the mess right now!"

60
00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:58.698
said Mrs.

61
00:03:58.798 --> 00:04:02.020
O'Donnell. She looked at the rest of us.

62
00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.641
"Can you please help him?"

63
00:04:07.102 --> 00:04:11.904
Josh, Jenny, and I went downstairs with Caswell and cleaned up the eggs from the sidewalk.

64
00:04:14.244 --> 00:04:15.765
Mr. Calabria helped us.

65
00:04:15.785 --> 00:04:18.926
"I talked to the workmen," he said.

66
00:04:18.946 --> 00:04:22.248
"Our electricity will be back on tomorrow."

67
00:04:23.368 --> 00:04:24.209
I groaned.

68
00:04:25.129 --> 00:04:28.830
"That means another hot night," I thought.

69
00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:35.849
"At least we can have fun with Tufty," said Molly when we got back upstairs.

70
00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:43.491
That night my battery fan hummed on my dresser, blowing air around the room.

71
00:04:44.631 --> 00:04:47.832
From somewhere far away, I could hear another sound.

72
00:04:49.032 --> 00:04:50.473
Whoo! Whoo!

73
00:04:50.493 --> 00:04:53.353
"A train whistle?"

74
00:04:53.874 --> 00:04:54.874
I thought sleepily.

75
00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:58.535
"I never heard a train whistle from my room before."

76
00:04:59.855 --> 00:05:02.336
I should have known it wasn't a real train whistle.

77
00:05:03.673 --> 00:05:07.380
After all, it was coming from Molly's apartment, right across the hall!
